  "details": "Too many users feel pressured to scale back their creativity when it comes to avatar sounds, for fear of other users employing the only three tools they have to curate their experience with avatar sounds: Disabling avatar sounds entirely, reducing their volume globally, or blocking that avatar, none of which are ideal.\n\nTo better resolve this, add a slider for avatar sound volume when selecting a user, similar to voice volume. This way, a user can adjust the avatar sounds of one person without disrupting their own experience of other users and their avatar sounds; the one person who is an issue can simply be selected, have their avatar sound volume reduced, and that's that, no further tinkering, no blocking/hiding, no global muting.",
